# A bare `describe` at the top of a spec is sent to `main`, which RSpec's
# `expose_dsl_globally` (the default) gives its group methods, each sending
# the call on to `RSpec`. It answers `RSpec.describe`, as the written
# `RSpec.describe` does; it was residue, the receiver undetermined.
def spec/widget_spec.rb:1:1 status=resolved owner=RSpec via=main kind=declaration defined_via=rspec
def spec/widget_spec.rb:5:1 status=resolved owner=RSpec via=main
